ter":"p-block-elements","chapterGroup":"inorganic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":2,"paperId":"iit-jee-2012-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pwith-respect-to-graphite-and-diamond-which-of-the-statem-jee-advanced-chemistry-some-basic-concepts-of-chemistry-lnu4apacj3tnoog1","question":{"en":{"direction":null,"content":"<p>With respect to graphite and diamond, which of the statement(s) given below is(are) correct?</p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Graphite is harder than diamond."},{"identifier":"B","content":"Graphite has higher electrical conductivity than diamond."},{"identifier":"C","content":"Graphite has higher thermal conductivity than diamond."},{"identifier":"D","content":"Graphite has higher C-C bond order than diamond."}],"correct_options":["B","D"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Diamond is hard and graphite is soft. Graphite is a good conductor of electricity as it has one free electron which is responsible for the conduction.</p>\n<p>Diamond has higher thermal conductivity than graphite because the structure of diamond is precise and thus the transfer of heat is faster in it.</p>\n<p>In case of graphite, the C-C bond has a double bond character so its bond order becomes higher than that of diamond which has only single C-C bonds.</p>"}},"subject":"chemistry","subjectGroup":null,"timeAllotted":180000,"topic":"group-14-elements-carbon-family","type":"mcqm","year":2012,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"isBonus":false,"yearKey":"iit-jee-2012-paper-2-offline","active":true},{"question_id":"1l23i26fs","chapter":"surface-chemistry","chapterGroup":"physical-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"medium","exam":"jee-advanced","examGroup":"jee","languages":["en"],"marks":4,"negMarks":2,"paperId":"iit-jee-2012-paper-2-offline","paperTitle":"IIT-JEE 2012 Paper 2 Offline","permalink":"pthe-given-graphsdata-i-ii-iii-and-iv-represent-