-1l26aq51q.png?format=png 500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/750/image/1l26aq51p/cc2cd976-0900-4be7-b19d-f4555fdb702e/b2d742e0-bff4-11ec-9807-3fb7842b4dc6/file-1l26aq51q.png?format=png 750w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1000/image/1l26aq51p/cc2cd976-0900-4be7-b19d-f4555fdb702e/b2d742e0-bff4-11ec-9807-3fb7842b4dc6/file-1l26aq51q.png?format=png 1000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/1500/image/1l26aq51p/cc2cd976-0900-4be7-b19d-f4555fdb702e/b2d742e0-bff4-11ec-9807-3fb7842b4dc6/file-1l26aq51q.png?format=png 1500w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2000/image/1l26aq51p/cc2cd976-0900-4be7-b19d-f4555fdb702e/b2d742e0-bff4-11ec-9807-3fb7842b4dc6/file-1l26aq51q.png?format=png 2000w, https://app-content.cdn.examgoal.net/fly/2500/image/1l26aq51p/cc2cd976-0900-4be7-b19d-f4555fdb702e/b2d742e0-bff4-11ec-9807-3fb7842b4dc6/file-1l26aq51q.png?format=png 2500w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 767px) 100vw, 720px\" decoding=\"async\"></p>","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"I is physisorption and II is chemisorption."},{"identifier":"B","content":"I is physisorption and III is chemisorption."},{"identifier":"C","content":"IV is chemisorption and II is chemisorption."},{"identifier":"D","content":"IV is chemisorption and III is chemisorption."}],"correct_options":["A","C"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>In the case of physiorption, with the increase of temperature and pressure the rate of adsorption decreases because according to Le Chatelier's principle, increase of temperature and pressure will shift the equilibrium to the left</p>\n<p>Adsorbate + Adsorbent <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.032ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"2.262ex\" height=\"1.195ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -514 1000 528\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\